Notebook[{Cell["TensorProductVectors", "ObjectName"], 
  Cell["TensorProductVectors[g, {v1, v2, ...}] multiplies \
representation-valued vectors left-associatively through CG duals, keeping \
every copy and every zero; TargetIrreps prunes the paths to the requested \
final irreps. {} gives the tensor unit.", "Usage"], 
  Cell["Status: Alpha.", "Notes"], Cell["TensorProductVectors[g, {v1, v2, \
...}] multiplies representation-valued vectors left-associatively through CG \
duals: every copy and every zero is kept and each record's path names its \
contractions. TargetIrreps prunes the paths to the requested final irreps, \
computing only the CG coefficients needed.", "Notes"], 
  Cell["{} gives the tensor unit (the trivial irrep with component 1). The \
vectors must share one frozen context; a group whose stored basis changed \
since they were made fails with StaleBasis (use their RepresentationContext). \
Components multiply commutatively.", "Notes"], 
